#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Fulda Gap: Hesse, November 1983.  A sample game for the Grognard
engine, and a war that never happened.

In November 1983 NATO rehearsed the release of its nuclear weapons in a
command post exercise called Able Archer 83, and in Moscow some feared
the exercise was cover for a real first strike.  Here they act on the
fear: the Group of Soviet Forces in Germany attacks first, without
nuclear weapons, through the Fulda Gap toward Frankfurt.  Play either
side against the computer, or against a friend at the same screen.

Run it with ./fulda (Python 3 with Tk, nothing else).  The game is
saved to ~/.fulda.json.  ./fulda --selftest checks the map and plays a
game between two computer players.
"""

